\title{Dexter2 Specification and Verification}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2025-09-06}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    Dexter2 has been formally verified by three different groups, using three different verification
    tools. These are:
    \ol{
        \li{Runtime Verification, using K Framework:
        [link](https://runtimeverification.com/blog/dexter-2-s-formal-verification)}
        \li{Nomadic Labs, using Mi-Cho-Coq:
        [link](https://gitlab.com/nomadic-labs/mi-cho-coq/-/merge_requests/100)}
        \li{Bas Spitters' team, using ConCert: [link](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2203.08016)}
    }
    Each is based on the same informal specification:
    [link](https://gitlab.com/dexter2tz/dexter2tz/-/blob/master/docs/informal-spec/dexter2-cpmm.md)
}

\p{
    For an analysis on similarities and differences, see the Introduction and Chapter 2 of my
    [PhD](dhsorens-phd) [thesis](/docs/sorensen-phd-thesis.pdf).
}